#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Build research/amm-multi-hop-split-boost-tf-multi-user-pool-chains-20261029 receipts.

3rd run packet #93: the split x boost x tf chain at TRUE 3 hops
(three_amm only, final output U3) meets a second user and a second chain.
Every sequence is pinned fresh on this chain: consecutive trades
and the price drift they leave behind, liquidity then trade (and
the reverse), sweep/collect then trade (and the reverse), boost
window transitions across repeated boosts and interleaved trades,
claim and lifecycle transitions (claim twice, sync then claim,
close then re-init then claim, extend then claim), setter then
trade transitions (buyback-config, fee-config, disable, toggles,
admin rotation, coin-creator set), failure rollback completeness
(the failed leg leaves every watched account byte-identical, and
the anchor leg after it still pays the anchor), order dependence
(the same legs in a different order end in different states, or
provably the same state), and withheld recovery transitions
(harvest then withdraw-from-mint after trades and sweeps).

MEASURE=1 prints MEAS lines; /tmp/meas2expect93.py turns them into
EXPECTS. Without MEASURE it writes the packet (receipts in 10-receipt
parts, report.json.gz) and prints the addresses verify.py needs.
"""
